   "textLength": 410,
   "text": "Employment verification is a standard part of securing a mortgage, giving lenders the ability to assess whether you can reliably make monthly payments. The borrower signs a form authorizing an employer to release employment and income information to a prospective lender, and from there, the lender typically calls the employer directly to obtain the necessary information, such as recent income docu",
